\tag{fdip}
\title{Scaling directions}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The coefficient shift in \ref{fdip-01CL} fixes the precision after
one blocking step. To compare changes at successive depths, a
perturbation must also be specified at every depth. Which such families
grow under the step, which stay unchanged, and which shrink?}

\p{Powers of the [nonnegative hierarchical Laplacian](fdip-01CQ) give operator
families to compare. For polynomial interactions, averaging over the
discarded Gaussian fluctuation gives another linear step. Its action
on variance-adjusted powers of the field can be computed exactly.}

